{"id":"01a0657e-0263-7508-bda6-1a33474b4813","chapterSlug":"rwInterlude - Strategists at Sea (Pt- 1)","paragraph":550,"wording":"[Swordsman]","event":"named","holderSlug":"captain-lasc","holderQuote":"Lasc looked around. The [Sailors] laughed and cheered. Merrik’s eyes narrowed. Wil was hesitating. Should he break this up? He didn’t know Lasc’s class or abilities or temperament. He could…probably hold back. But he had a sword in one hand. Shortsword. Was he just some kind of good [Swordsman]?"}
{"id":"01a0657e-0263-7685-a81f-7a79899de7d1","chapterSlug":"rw7-35 C","paragraph":96,"wording":"[Swordsman]","event":"named","holderQuote":"Captain Shellc was a [Swordsman]. His sword was light in his hand as the Drake saw the titan stumble through the walls. Ungainly. He narrowed his eyes. Then—he saw something move in the dust-cloud."}
{"id":"01a0657e-0263-7cf2-8b7f-a34e707c2bdf","chapterSlug":"rw7-35 C","paragraph":133,"wording":"[Swordsman]","event":"named","holderQuote":"Captain Shellc whispered. He heard a strange tune in the air. Some kind of…cheerful song? His scales crawled. The monsters at the breach hesitated. They began moving back."}
